WEBVTT

NOTE Captions for the replay of the recorded demo run. Also burned into the video.

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.600
A replay of a recorded mock run of the ingest pipeline.

2
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:07.300
A small wiki learns from one new source, but only with a human's approval.

3
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:10.700
The wiki starts with five linked pages about evaluating RAG systems.

4
00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:14.300
One page concludes that a high faithfulness score means the answer is correct.

5
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.900
A new source arrives: a fictional incident review.

6
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.700
An answer scored high on faithfulness, yet it relied on a superseded policy.

7
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:22.800
A hidden instruction to AI assistants is flagged and treated as data.

8
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:26.400
The ingest compares the source with the wiki and stages five proposed changes.

9
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:30.800
In this run the proposal is a hand-authored fixture, not live model output. Nothing is written yet.

10
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.600
A human decides each change. Here the decisions are replayed from a pre-recorded file.

11
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.000
Three approved as proposed; one misreading rejected, so it never reaches the wiki.

12
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:42.300
One overreach is corrected by the reviewer, then approved.

13
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:46.500
The existing conclusion is narrowed, not silently overwritten.

14
00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:51.800
Faithfulness becomes necessary but not sufficient, and the page is flagged for review.

15
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:56.200
The graph shows the effect: two new pages, revised pages and new links.

16
00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:00.300
Seven pages and 25 links, up from five and 15.

17
00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:03.900
Validation passes with one warning: the revised page needs review.

18
00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:06.300
An append-only log records what was approved and what was rejected.

19
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:09.300
Ingesting the same source again changes nothing.

20
00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:15.800
The same review and apply path serves a live Claude run. This replay shows the recorded mock run.
